Priority: 2
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: fix-text-tool-commit-control, add-text-tool, add-selection-and-move-tools

Goal:
Allow existing canvas text items to be edited after placement.

Context:
The first-pass text tool created persistent text items, but re-editing was explicitly out of scope. The user now wants selected text to reopen an editor pre-filled with the existing content so they can delete, modify, or append text without recreating the item from scratch.

Expected changes:

- define the gesture that enters text re-edit mode for an existing text item
- when a text item is edited, show the same inline editor used for new text placement
- prefill the editor with the current text content
- on accept, update the existing text item in place instead of creating a duplicate
- preserve selection and positioning behavior around the edit flow

Acceptance criteria:

- Selecting an existing text item and invoking edit reopens a text editor at that item.
- The editor starts with the existing text already filled in.
- Accepting the edit updates the original text item instead of adding a new one.
- Deleting all text and accepting follows a defined behavior, either removing the item or leaving it unchanged, but not corrupting canvas state.
- `npm run build` and `cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` pass.

Notes:

- Reuse the same editor semantics established by `fix-text-tool-commit-control` so new and existing text behave consistently.
- Rich text and font-level styling remain out of scope.
